<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Google "G", at the 24dp the button draws it at.

  Four paths rather than one, because the mark IS four colours: the blue bar, the
  green lower arc, the yellow left arc and the red top arc. A single-tint
  version — which is what an icon font gives you — would be a different logo, and
  on a button whose whole job is to be recognised at a glance that is the one
  thing it must not be.

  Drawn as a vector so it needs no density buckets, and so the white surface
  behind it is the button's rather than baked into a bitmap.
-->
